{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"dirt-prior-falcon","creation_channel":"cli","description":"RP-04 S1 advisory review finding (change 1841 PS3): the AC1 cross-surface equivalence contract test (tests/interfaces/contracts/test_operation_snapshot_surfaces.py) asserts CLI/lib/MCP/reconciler snapshot equivalence, but the 'MCP surface' and 'reconciler surface' blocks call compose_operation_snapshot(...) directly again with identical args rather than driving the actual MCP tool and reconciler __main__ entry points. Strengthen so those two slots exercise the real surfaces (surface-parity: a surface that performs the op but does not route through the shared composer is exactly where a parity bug hides). Acceptance: the MCP and reconciler blocks invoke their real entry points; mutation-perturbing the composer makes the surface assertions RED.","id":"bbb7-812e-4fe4-465d","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Drive AC1 snapshot-equivalence contract through real MCP + reconciler entry points"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787015272752888001,"uuid":"58885abb-dd15-47d0-80c8-003b1a79d479"}